I am sitting on the bed.
I take the mobile phone.
I call my parents in Mexico.
"Hello Maya!" says my mother.
"How are you?" asks my father.
"Thanks, I am doing well," I say.
"Are you in Berlin?"
"Yes, I am in Berlin."
"Is it cold?" asks my mother.
"Yes, very cold," I answer.
"But the room is warm and everything is fine."
"What is there in the room?" asks my father.
"There is a bed, a table, and a lamp."
"Where are Diego and Sofia?" I ask.
"They are not here," says my mother.
"But Lola is here!"
I hear the dog and smile.
"I am very tired," I say.
"Good night, Maya!" say my parents.
